## The Yellow Stone Question

There is a split in search intent for this keyword that you need to understand.

Some buyers searching "emerald cut diamond ring yellow gold" want a yellow gold setting for a white diamond. Others are searching for a yellow diamond — specifically a canary yellow diamond — in an emerald cut. These are two completely different products at two completely different price points.

[![Emerald cut diamond solitaire ring in yellow gold tapered setting](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-solitaire-ring-yellow-gold-tapered.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=yg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Yellow gold setting for a white diamond:** This is what most buyers want — a standard 18K yellow gold ring setting from [around $935 for the Classic Comfort Fit](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-comfort-fit-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-203284?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) to [$5,190 for the dedicated EC setting](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/emerald-cut-diamond-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-203303?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), with a natural or lab-grown white diamond. Full ring from $4,075.

**Yellow diamond in an emerald cut:** A fancy yellow (canary) diamond in an emerald cut is a completely different product. Fancy yellow diamonds are rare — a 1ct fancy yellow emerald cut runs $5,000–$30,000+ depending on color intensity and cut quality. If this is what you are looking for, search for fancy colored diamonds specifically — the rings in this post are white diamonds in yellow gold settings only.

The Yellow Stone Question is worth naming because people spend time in the wrong part of the market. If you want yellow gold + white stone, you are in the right place. If you want a yellow diamond, no ring in this post applies.

