The range here is significant. From [the $935 Classic Comfort Fit](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-comfort-fit-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-203284?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) to [the $5,190 dedicated EC setting](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/emerald-cut-diamond-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-203303?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a $4,255 gap in the setting alone. Most buyers get the same visual result — an emerald cut solitaire in yellow gold — from either end of that range.

The settings in the $935–$1,400 range have the most reviews for a reason. Buyers who actually purchase these rings are not choosing the most expensive settings. They are choosing the settings that let the stone be the focal point.

