EC-specific settings cost more because they require custom tooling for the rectangular stone shape. The prongs on a purpose-built EC setting grip the corners precisely — not the sides, which would block the step-cut facets. For a [bezel-set emerald cut](/bezel-set-emerald-cut-diamond-ring), the metal lip follows the exact rectangular outline of the stone.

The low review counts here (1–13 reviews) do not indicate poor quality. EC-specific settings serve a smaller volume category — fewer people buy them per month, so fewer people review them. The build quality on purpose-built EC settings is typically higher than universal settings that have simply been adapted for the shape.

