## The 1186-Review Standard

In a market of hundreds of yellow gold settings, one setting dominates by review volume: the [Petite Solitaire YG at $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-195639?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), with 1,186 verified reviews.

That number is meaningful. Most engagement ring settings have under 100 reviews, and 500 is exceptional. 1,186 reviews is not a fluke — it means buyers choose this setting consistently, at scale, across different stones and different budgets.

The Petite Solitaire YG is The 1186-Review Standard because it represents the real-world verdict of over a thousand emerald cut purchases.

[![Emerald cut diamond ring yellow gold pavé halo setting on model](/images/emerald-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-pave-halo.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=yg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

What does that verdict say? Buyers want a clean four-prong solitaire in yellow gold — slender band, full stone visibility, no competing shapes. They are not spending [$2,000–$5,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=yg&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) on a setting when [$1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-item-195639?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives them the same result.

The Petite Pavé Lab-Grown YG with 1,150 reviews says a slightly different thing. Buyers who choose lab stones also want the yellow gold band, but they add fine pavé for additional sparkle on the shoulders. At [$1,400](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-pave-engagement-ring-in-18k-yellow-gold-lab-grown-item-315084?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), it is a $400 premium over the plain solitaire — and 1,150 buyers found that premium worth it.

The 1186-Review Standard does not mean every buyer should choose the Petite Solitaire. It means if you want market validation, this setting has more of it than anything else in the category. Pick a setting with 11 reviews and you are pioneering — pick this one and you are buying with the crowd.

> **Farzana says:** "When a client asks me which yellow gold setting is safest, I tell them to look at the review count first. Not the price, not the design description. The review count tells you what real buyers are actually choosing. 1,186 people picked the Petite Solitaire in yellow gold. That is not a coincidence — that is a consensus."

